  "observation": "Zoom makes scientific operator and implementation mapping separable: whole-pixel interval means are not bilinear or overlap-weighted resampling, and output dimensions remain fixed through crop/pad. A geometry-based unit-cell intersection oracle computes exact rational means at actual Float32 endpoints, independently of the shared implementation and native CPU loops. Constant fields remain exactly one in every measured output, and all edge/crop pixels are checked. Source-backed tile capacities and pipeline stage count provide analysis traits; no causal shared-memory bottleneck claim follows from small-case timings.",
